    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know they aren't permanent but it's not just a 'crisis' to me. it's like my entire soul was tied to my presence online. now that's gone, there's nothing left inside. it’s like the shell is just moving through the motions but the real person—the one who mattered—is just dead. how am i supposed to just 'rebuild' when the foundation was everything?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that losing a significant part of your perceived self, especially when tied to a public presence, feels like catastrophic loss. When the foundation feels gone, the focus needs to shift from \"rebuilding\" the old structure to gently discovering what remains within itself. Start small by acknowledging the small, quiet things you still feel, notice, or do that are intrinsically yours, separate from any previous online persona. Allow yourself time to mourn what has been lost before you pressure yourself to define what comes next.",
      "source": "target",
